{
  "name": "330. Every error carries extra_fields.error_type (fork error types)",
  "description": "Contract C6 (Bifrost-Tokun, BF8/BF9): every error response carries extra_fields.error_type from the closed vocabulary, so a client classifies a failure by one field and never by its text. A governance refusal is policy_*, never provider_auth_failed although it is a 401/403. A route that answers in a vendor-native error envelope (/anthropic/v1/messages) has no extra_fields, so the x-bifrost-error-type header carries the same value on every error. A vendor 403 content block is caller_content_filtered and is not a key failure: it reaches the upstream once (no same-key retry, no rotation). A speech 200 with no audio and no error object is 502 provider_empty_result, with the vendor headers kept. The fixture cases run only against the provider error fixture. A vendor-call error carries upstream_sent from the shared HTTP client (TXE-6746): false when the connection was refused before any byte was written, true once the vendor answered, and true for the call when any fallback attempt was sent.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "330.1 [EXPECT-401] openai/gpt-4o-mini an unknown virtual key is policy_access_denied, not provider_auth_failed (fork error types)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "x-bf-vk",
            "value": "sk-bf-harness-error-type-unknown"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o-mini\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"hi\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"max_tokens\": 8\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "chat",
            "completions"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('401 refusal carries policy_access_denied in the body and the header', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(401);",
              "  var j = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(j.extra_fields && j.extra_fields.error_type, 'error_type: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql('policy_access_denied');",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('x-bifrost-error-type'), 'header').to.eql('policy_access_denied');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
